findings.comment:
Observed a deep container of sliced tomatoes (which are a Time/Temperature Control for Safety Food) which was measured at 47°F (probed), above 41°F. Tomatoes were prepared beyond the 4 hour cooling window to use time as a control. Other items in the fridge were sufficiently cold holding. CORRECTED: PIC voluntarily discarded the tomatoes. Inspector discussed with PIC and staff solutions for cooling prepared TCS produce:
(i) preparing smaller amounts of food that will cool faster; 
(ii) preparing shallower containers or smaller containers so that food can more easily disperse heat and cool faster; 
(iii) cooling the tomatoes in the walk-in cooler, which cools food more effectively, especially as the standing cooler in the kitchen area is frequently opened during service, making cooling difficult. 
(iv) store whole tomatoes under refrigeration to pre-cool them prior to cutting.
Ensure that all TCS Foods are cooled within 4 hours to 41°F or less when prepared from ingredients at ambient temperature.
